  "summary": "Timeline bands reorganised. Four bands, top to bottom: Historians (new; person entries who mainly write history), Schools and fields (the former schools, approaches and expanding fields with the enduring fields and genres folded in), Theorists (philosophers and social, cultural and literary theorists), and Traditions and theories (the earlier intellectual traditions with six theory groups moved from the thinkers band; the c. 1920 cut-off leaves the name). Band ids are kept where they continue, so links and the archived 2000 view still work.",
  "authorization": "User, 2026-10-19: \"I think we probably want to reorganize the whole timeline\"; \"historians should be distinct from theorist\"; \"Enduring Fields & Geners should be folded into Schools, Approaches and Expanding fields with a simpler name\"; \"historians should be at the top\"; order Historians · Schools and fields · Theorists · Traditions and theories; theory groups join the traditions band; Kuhn a historian; \"Rachel Carson and Aldo Leopold are not historians\".",
  "rationale": "The thinkers band mixed historians, theorists and six theory groups (Frankfurt School, British cultural studies, structural linguistics, practice theory, historical epistemology, the explanation and objectivity debates). The person classification is in person-classification.csv (77 historians, 21 theorists), with the contested calls marked and the user's decisions recorded.",
